= Validation set — Simple =

A '''validation set''' is data used while developing a machine-learning system.

The model does not normally learn its main parameters directly from these examples.

Instead, developers use validation results to choose settings, models, thresholds, or when to stop training.

Because developers look at validation results many times, they can accidentally overfit to the validation set.

That is why a separate test set is useful for final evaluation.

